2 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329947 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186329507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329947 #edb/ref 1069 "q-48993" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329947 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329947 #edb/ref 1071 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=e.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329947 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4a6705a9-7a56-57af-9eab-fa453a263686" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329947 #edb/ref 1074 "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=e$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=e} & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡e \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336092 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336092 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336092 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "07b1c5dd-3548-52e8-9ae9-7a7e69e1cbd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336121 #edb/ref 1080 "12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336121 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336121 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "09ea4053-49e8-5168-b098-82430469625d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336321 #edb/ref 1080 "-9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336321 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 1759218604